Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Special Act on the Creation of Yongsan Park and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of the Main Site, etc.)
(1) "Sites prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3, subparagraph 1(a) of the Special Act on the Creation of Yongsan Park (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means sites located in Yongsan-dong 1-ga, 2-ga, 3-ga, 4-ga, 5-ga, and 6-ga and Seobinggo-dong, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, which the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport publicly notifies in consultation with the Minister of National Defense after conducting a basic survey pursuant to Article 10 of the Act. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
(2) "Sites prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3, subparagraph 1(b) of the Act means sites located in Hangangno 1-ga, Itaewon-dong, and Dongbinggo-dong, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, which the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport publicly notifies in consultation with the Minister of National Defense after conducting a basic survey pursuant to Article 10 of the Act. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>

Article 3 (Operation of the Yongsan Park Creation Promotion Committee)
(1) The chairperson shall convene and preside over meetings of the Yongsan Park Creation Promotion Committee under Article 7(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee").
(2) A meeting of the Committee shall open with the attendance of a majority of its incumbent members and adopt resolutions by the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(3) The Committee shall have one secretary, who shall be the head of the Yongsan Park Creation Promotion Planning Group under Article 8.

Article 4 (Subcommittees)
(1) The Committee may establish subcommittees to perform its duties efficiently.
(2) A subcommittee shall consist of no more than seven non-governmental members from among the members of the Committee, and the chairperson of a subcommittee shall be elected by and from among its members.

Article 5 (Requests for Cooperation from Relevant Institutions, etc.)
(1) Where necessary for the performance of its duties, the Committee may request necessary cooperation, such as having relevant public officials or experts attend meetings of the Committee to hear their opinions, or having the heads of relevant administrative agencies or relevant institutions, corporations, organizations, etc. submit materials or opinions.
(2) Where necessary for the performance of its duties, the Committee may gather public opinion by holding public hearings or seminars, conducting broadcast discussions, or other means.

Article 6 (Allowances)
Non-governmental members of the Committee or subcommittees, and relevant experts and others attending meetings, may be paid allowances, travel expenses, and other necessary expenses within budgetary limits.

Article 7 (Detailed Rules for Operation)
Except as provided in this Decree, matters necessary for the operation of the Committee and subcommittees shall be determined by the chairperson who is the Prime Minister following a resolution of the Committee. <Amended 2009.6.25, 2013.3.23, 2019.9.24>

Article 8 (Composition and Operation of the Yongsan Park Creation Promotion Planning Group)
(1) The Yongsan Park Creation Promotion Planning Group under Article 9 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Planning Group") shall consist of one head and members, and the position of head shall be filled by a public official belonging to the Senior Civil Service.
(2) The head of the Planning Group shall handle its affairs under the direction of the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended 2009.6.25, 2013.3.23, 2019.9.24>
(3) Where necessary for the performance of the Planning Group's duties, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request the secondment of public officials from relevant administrative agencies or officers, employees, or other personnel of relevant organizations. <Amended 2009.6.25, 2013.3.23, 2019.9.24>
(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), matters necessary for the composition, operation, etc. of the Planning Group shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended 2009.6.25, 2013.3.23, 2019.9.24>

Article 9 (Formulation of Basic Survey Plans)
The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall formulate a basic survey plan before conducting a basic survey pursuant to Article 10 of the Act.

Article 10 (Minor Changes to the Yongsan Park Improvement Area)
"Where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are changed" in the proviso to Article 11(5) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the area of the Yongsan Park Creation District is changed by less than 3,000 square meters (a total area of less than 5,000 square meters where changes are made twice or more);
2. Where a change is made within 10 percent of the area of a mixed-use facilities creation district or an area surrounding the park;
3. Where the area or boundaries of the Yongsan Park Improvement Area are changed to correct errors or omissions or as a result of a survey.

Article 11 (Formulation, etc. of Comprehensive Master Plans)
(1) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13(2)5 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters concerning the basic direction for the management and improvement of areas surrounding the park;
2. Matters concerning the direction for formulating the Yongsan Park Creation Plan and mixed-use facilities creation plans;
3. Matters concerning the basic direction for handling proceeds from mixed-use facilities creation projects;
4. Matters concerning the area of the Yongsan Park Improvement Area;
5. Other matters necessary for the efficient creation and management of the Yongsan Park Improvement Area.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has formulated a comprehensive master plan under Article 13(1) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
1. Matters referred to in subparagraphs 1 through 4 of Article 13(2) of the Act;
2. Matters referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).
(3) "Where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are changed" in the proviso to Article 13(5) of the Act means cases falling under the subparagraphs of Article 10.
(4) Before publicly notifying the comprehensive master plan under paragraph (2), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall consult with the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment on a strategic environmental impact assessment under Article 9 of the Environmental Impact Assessment Act. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2012.7.20, 2013.3.23, 2025.10.1>

Article 12 (Formulation of the Yongsan Park Creation Plan)
(1) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 14(3)10 of the Act means the following matters: <Amended 2024.5.7>
1. Matters concerning plans for the preservation of national heritage within the Yongsan Park Creation District;
2. Matters concerning the phased implementation of the Yongsan Park Creation Plan;
3. The locations, lot numbers, land categories, and areas of land, objects, and rights (hereinafter referred to as "land, etc.") to be expropriated or used; particulars of ownership and rights other than ownership; and the names (in the case of corporations, corporate names) and addresses of their owners and right holders.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has formulated a Yongsan Park Creation Plan under Article 14(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Yongsan Park Creation Plan"), the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended 2008.2.29, 2012.4.10, 2013.3.23>
1. The name and purpose of the project;
2. The location and area of the Yongsan Park Creation District and the project implementation period;
3. Matters concerning land use plans and infrastructure installation plans;
4. Matters concerning the determination of urban or Gun management plans;
5. The locations, lot numbers, land categories, and areas of land, etc. to be expropriated or used; particulars of ownership and rights other than ownership; and the names (in the case of corporations, corporate names) and addresses of their owners and right holders;
6. Methods for inspecting relevant documents and drawings.
(3) "Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 14(7) of the Act means the following changes:
1. Changes in the name of the project and the project implementation period;
2. A change within 10 percent of the cost of the Yongsan Park creation project;
3. A change within 10 percent of the site area of Yongsan Park facilities;
4. Changes in the area and boundaries of the Yongsan Park Creation District to correct errors or omissions or as a result of a survey.

Article 13 (Designation of Park Creation Project Implementers)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to designate a park creation project implementer under Article 15(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "park creation project implementer"), the Minister shall take the following matters into consideration: <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23, 2021.11.11>
1. The details and scale of the project under the Yongsan Park Creation Plan;
2. The ability to procure financial resources;
3. The purpose of establishment and implementation capabilities of a public corporation under Article 5(4)1 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions (hereinafter referred to as a "public corporation").
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has designated a park creation project implementer pursuant to Article 15(1) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
1. The name, outline, and implementation period of the project;
2. The name (including the name of its representative) and address of the park creation project implementer;
3. The location and area of the project implementation area.

Article 14 (Preparation, etc. of Implementation Plans for the Creation of Yongsan Park)
(1) A park creation project implementer designated pursuant to Article 15(1) of the Act shall prepare an implementation plan for the creation of Yongsan Park under Article 16(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan") in conformity with the Yongsan Park Creation Plan.
(2) Where a park creation project implementer intends to obtain approval for an implementation plan, the implementer shall submit an application for approval prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents. In such cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall verify the cadastral map of the project implementation area through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2008.12.31, 2010.5.4, 2012.4.10, 2013.3.23>
1. A plan drawing and schematic design documents;
2. A financing plan (including a plan for the input of funds by year);
3. A location map of the project implementation area;
4. A purchase plan and a compensation plan for land, etc. (including relocation measures, etc. under Article 53 of the Act);
5. A statement of existing buildings, structures, etc. intended to be retained;
6. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for the determination of urban or Gun management plans;
7. Documents necessary for consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies under Article 17(2) of the Act.
(3) "Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 16(5) of the Act means any of the following changes:
1. Changes in the address and representative of the park creation project implementer;
2. A change within 10 percent of the approved installation area of equipment or facilities;
3. A change in the layout of park facilities within a scope that does not depart from the finalized Yongsan Park Creation Plan;
4. Any of the changes referred to in subparagraphs 2 through 4 of Article 12(3).

Article 15 (Public Notice of Implementation Plans)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport approves an implementation plan pursuant to Article 16(1) of the Act, the Minister shall give public notice of the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on February 29, 2008; April 10, 2012; March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the project;
2. The name (including the name of its representative) and address of the park creation project implementer;
3. The location and area of the Yongsan Park Creation District and the project implementation period;
4. The details of the decision on the urban/Gun management plan;
5. Matters concerning public notices and public announcements of authorizations, permissions, etc. deemed granted by giving public notice of the implementation plan pursuant to Article 17 of the Act;
6. The method for inspecting the relevant documents and drawings;
7. The location, lot number, land category, and area of the land, etc. to be expropriated, details of ownership and rights other than ownership, and the names (in the case of corporations, their corporate names) and addresses of the owners and rights holders: Provided, That these may be omitted where they are the same as the contents of the Yongsan Park Creation Plan publicly notified pursuant to Article 14(5) of the Act, but the fact of their omission shall be clearly indicated.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport gives public notice of an implementation plan pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall send copies of the relevant documents to the Mayor of Seoul Special Metropolitan City. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(3) The Mayor of Seoul Special Metropolitan City shall make the copies of the relevant documents received pursuant to paragraph (2) available for public inspection.

Article 16 (Completion Inspections)
(1) Where a park creation project implementer intends to undergo a completion inspection after completing all or part of a project for the creation of the Yongsan Park Creation District pursuant to Article 19(1) of the Act, the implementer shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. A statement of completion;
2. A statement of land areas by use and a plan drawing;
3. Documents necessary for consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies under Article 19(4) of the Act;
4. A statement and drawings showing the vesting of public facilities, etc. under Article 52 of the Act;
5. A comparative map of the old and new cadastres and a map showing cadastral survey results;
6. A statement of the areas of dual-purpose structures under Article 23 of the Act on Urban Parks, Green Areas, Etc., classified by manager.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport completes a completion inspection pursuant to Article 19(6) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly announce the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the project;
2. The location and area of the Yongsan Park Creation District;
3. The name (including the name of its representative) and address of the park creation project implementer;
4. The date of completion;
5. Matters concerning the management and disposition of facilities, etc.

Article 17 Deleted. <November 11, 2021>

Article 18 (Prohibited Activities in Yongsan Park)
(1) The term "activities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(1)5 of the Act means the following activities: <Amended on November 11, 2021>
1. Entering Yongsan Park without putting an accompanying companion animal on a leash that allows it to be controlled;
2. Leaving excrement from an accompanying companion animal uncollected.
(2) The term "activities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(1)6 of the Act means the following activities:
1. Camping, cooking, or lighting a fire in a place other than a designated place;
2. Gambling or similar activities;
3. Dumping filth or waste in a place other than a designated place;
4. Parking in a place other than a designated place;
5. Entering or leaving a place other than a roadway using a motorized device with two or more wheels: Provided, That this shall exclude entry or exit by persons with disabilities or elderly or infirm persons using chair vehicles for persons with physical disabilities, such as wheelchairs, under subparagraph 16 of Article 2 of the Road Traffic Act;
6. Collecting flowers or fruit from plants without authorization;
7. Abusing animals inhabiting the park or capturing them without obtaining permission, etc.;
8. Releasing non-native animals that could disrupt the park ecosystem.

Article 19 (Applications for Permission for Occupancy and Use of Yongsan Park)
A person intending to obtain permission for occupancy and use of Yongsan Park pursuant to Article 23(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. A project plan (including a location map and a plan drawing);
2. A construction implementation plan;
3. A plan for restoration to the original condition.

Article 20 (Scope of and Criteria for Permission for Occupancy and Use)
(1) The matters subject to permission for occupancy and use of Yongsan Park under Article 23(1) of the Act shall be as set forth in Attached Table 1.
(2) The criteria for permission for occupancy and use of Yongsan Park under Article 23(1) of the Act shall be as set forth in Attached Table 2.

Article 21 (Mixed-Use Facilities Creation Plans)
(1) Where a project implementer for the creation of mixed-use facilities under Article 26(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "mixed-use facilities project implementer") intends to obtain approval for a mixed-use facilities creation plan under Article 25(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "mixed-use facilities creation plan"), the implementer shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for approval prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the mixed-use facilities creation plan. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) The term "other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25(2)9 of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on April 10, 2012; May 7, 2024>
1. Plans for the installation of major infrastructure, such as roads, water supply systems, and sewerage systems;
2. Plans for the supply of integrated energy;
3. Plans for underground installations, such as common utility ducts;
4. Plans for the preservation of national heritage within the mixed-use facilities creation district;
5. Matters concerning the urban/Gun management plan.
(3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport approves a mixed-use facilities creation plan pursuant to Article 25(4) of the Act, the Minister shall give public notice of the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on February 29, 2008; April 10, 2012; March 23, 2013>
1. The name and purpose of the project and the mixed-use facilities project implementer;
2. The location and area of the mixed-use facilities creation district and the project implementation period;
3. Matters concerning the land use plan and infrastructure installation plan;
4. Matters concerning the decision on the urban/Gun management plan;
5. The method for inspecting the relevant documents and drawings.
(4) The term "changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 25(6) of the Act means any of the following changes:
1. A change in the name of the project, the project implementation period, or the address or representative of the implementer;
2. A change of no more than 10/100 in the cost of the project for the creation of mixed-use facilities;
3. A change in the land use plan within a range of 10/100 of the land area for each major use;
4. A change of no more than 10/100 in the area of infrastructure, such as roads;
5. A change of no more than 10/100 in the respective areas for installing equipment and facilities;
6. A minor change to the comprehensive master plan under Article 11(3).

Article 22 (Mixed-Use Facilities Project Implementers)
(1) The term "public corporations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 26(1)1 of the Act means public corporations capable of performing the following duties: <Amended on April 10, 2012>
1. Projects for urban/Gun planning facilities;
2. Projects for the creation, improvement, and development of cities;
3. Projects for the creation and development of commercial, office, residential, cultural, or other facilities;
4. Projects to construct housing or buildings for official or public use;
5. Other projects similar to those under subparagraphs 1 through 4.
(2) The term "corporations meeting the requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 26(1)2 of the Act means corporations in which the equity contribution ratio of private business operators is less than 50/100.

Article 23 (Applications for Designation as Mixed-Use Facilities Project Implementers, Etc.)
(1) A person intending to be designated as a mixed-use facilities project implementer shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for designation prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents and drawings: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; June 3, 2014>
1. A location map of the area in which the project for the creation of mixed-use facilities is to be implemented;
2. A project plan;
3. A financing plan (including a plan for committing funds by year);
4. A certificate of land ownership, written consent to the use of land, or documents proving that the land will be transferred without charge (granted) in the future.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport designates a mixed-use facilities project implementer, the Minister shall give public notice of the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The name (including the name of its representative) and address of the mixed-use facilities project implementer;
2. The name, outline, and implementation period of the project;
3. The location and area of the area in which the project is to be implemented.

Article 24 (Applications for Approval of Implementation Plans for the Creation of Mixed-Use Facilities, Etc.)
(1) Where a project implementer for the creation of mixed-use facilities intends to obtain approval for an implementation plan for the creation of mixed-use facilities pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act, the implementer shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for approval prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents. In such cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall check the cadastral map of the area in which the project is to be implemented through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; December 31, 2008; May 4, 2010; April 10, 2012; March 23, 2013>
1. Layout plans and schematic design documents;
2. A financing plan (including a plan for committing funds by year);
3. A location map of the area in which the project is to be implemented;
4. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for a decision on the urban/Gun management plan;
5. Documents necessary for consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies pursuant to Article 27(2) of the Act;
6. Detailed statements of public facilities, etc. under Article 52 of the Act and plans for their disposition.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport approves an implementation plan for the creation of mixed-use facilities under Article 27(1) of the Act, the Minister shall give public notice of the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on February 29, 2008; April 10, 2012; March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the project;
2. The location and area of the area in which the project for the creation of mixed-use facilities is to be implemented and the project implementation period;
3. The name (including the name of its representative) and address of the project implementer for the creation of mixed-use facilities;
4. The details of the decision on the urban/Gun management plan;
5. Matters concerning public notices or public announcements of authorizations, permissions, etc. deemed granted by giving public notice of approval of the implementation plan pursuant to Article 28(1) of the Act;
6. The method for inspecting the relevant documents and drawings.
(3) The term "changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 27(4) of the Act means changes falling under any subparagraph of Article 21(4).

Article 25 (Bearing of Costs)
(1) The costs that the State may require the Seoul Metropolitan Government to bear pursuant to Article 42 (1) of the Act shall be part of the construction costs directly necessary for the establishment of Yongsan Park and Yongsan Park facilities (meaning the sum of material costs, labor costs, expenses, general administrative expenses, and profit under Article 9 (1) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Contracts to Which the State Is a Party).
(2) The share of costs to be borne by the Seoul Metropolitan Government pursuant to the proviso to Article 42 (1) of the Act and other relevant matters shall be determined through consultation between the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and the Mayor of Seoul Metropolitan Government. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>

Article 26 (Formulation of Relocation Measures, etc.)
(1) Relocation measures and other measures under Article 53 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "relocation measures, etc.") shall include the following matters. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
1. Methods for implementing relocation measures under Article 78 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects and criteria for selecting eligible persons;
2. The timing, methods, recipients, procedures, and conditions for supplying land and other resources necessary for livelihood measures, taking into account the original ownership of land and other property and the means of livelihood of residents living in the Yongsan Park Creation District;
3. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for the resettlement of residents.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to formulate relocation measures, etc., the Minister shall hear the opinions of residents' representatives and the Mayor of Seoul Metropolitan Government. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
(3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may separately determine matters necessary to efficiently carry out the formulation and implementation of relocation measures, etc. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>

Article 26-2 (Entrustment of Authority or Affairs)
(1) Pursuant to Article 57-3 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall entrust the following affairs to the Yongsan Park Management Center under Article 31 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Management Center"):
1. Enforcement against prohibited acts under Article 22 of the Act;
2. Receipt of applications for permission for occupancy and use under Article 23 of the Act;
3. Management of dual-purpose structures under Article 23 of the Act on Urban Parks and Green Areas, which applies mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 24 of the Act;
4. Consultation concerning the bearing of costs incurred in managing dual-purpose structures under Article 42 (2) of the Act;
5. Collection of fees for using Yongsan Park facilities under Article 43 of the Act;
6. Collection of occupancy and use fees for Yongsan Park under Article 44 of the Act.
(2) Pursuant to Article 57-3 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may entrust preliminary surveys under Article 10 of the Act and investigations and the preparation and preservation of records under Article 57-2 of the Act to the following institutions. <Amended 2024.5.7>
1. Public enterprises;
2. Government-funded research institutes under Article 2 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes or government-funded science and technology research institutes under Article 2 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
3. Academic societies or corporations related to urban affairs, the environment, landscape architecture, architecture, civil engineering, society, or culture;
4. Buried heritage inspection institutions under Article 24 (1) of the Act on Protection and Inspection of Buried Heritage;
5. Other institutions recognized by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as having expertise in preliminary surveys under Article 10 of the Act and investigations and the preparation and preservation of records under Article 57-2 of the Act that are necessary for the creation of Yongsan Park and mixed-use facilities.
(3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport entrusts affairs pursuant to paragraph (2), the Minister shall publicly notify the entrusted institution and the details of the entrusted affairs in the Official Gazette.

Article 26-3 (Processing of Personally Identifiable Information)
Where unavoidable for the performance of affairs concerning verification of grounds for disqualification under Article 36 of the Act in connection with the appointment or removal of the chairperson or auditor of the Management Center under Article 35 of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or the Minister of Planning and Budget may process materials containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under Article 19, subparagraph 1 or 4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act. <Amended 2025.12.30>

Article 27 (Imposition and Collection of Administrative Fines)
(1) Where the chairperson of the Management Center or an employee thereof detects a violation within Yongsan Park that is subject to an administrative fine under Article 63 of the Act, the chairperson or employee shall notify the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, furnishing materials such as the offender's personal particulars and photographs, videotapes or other visual recording media, or photographs taken by unmanned enforcement equipment, together with documents stating the location and details of the violation and other relevant matters. <Amended 2008.2.29, 2013.3.23>
(2) Deleted. <2009.6.25>
(3) Deleted. <2009.6.25>
(4) The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 63 (1) and (2) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 3. <Amended 2009.6.25>
(5) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to impose an administrative fine under Article 63 (1), the Minister may reduce or increase the amount specified in attached Table 3 by up to one-half, taking into account the severity and number of the violations, their motives and consequences, and other relevant circumstances: Provided, That even where the amount is increased, it shall not exceed the maximum administrative fine under Article 63 (1) of the Act. <Amended 2009.6.25, 2013.3.23>

ADDENDA <No. 20508, 2007.12.31>

This Decree shall enter into force on January 1, 2008.

ADDENDA (Organization of the Ministry of Land, Transport and Maritime Affairs and Its Affiliated Agencies) <No. 20722, 2008.2.29>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation: Provided, That, among the Presidential Decrees amended pursuant to Article 6 of the Addenda, the provisions amending Presidential Decrees that were promulgated before this Decree enters into force but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective enforcement dates of those Presidential Decrees.

Articles 2 through 5 Omitted.

Article 6 (Amendment of Other Statutes and Regulations)
(1) through (79) Omitted.

(80) The Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on the Creation of Yongsan Park is partially amended as follows:

In Article 2 (1) and (2); the portion of Article 9 (1) preceding the subparagraphs and Article 9 (2); the portion of Article 11 (2) preceding the subparagraphs and Article 11 (4); the portion of Article 12 (2) preceding the subparagraphs; the portions of Article 13 (1) and (2) preceding the subparagraphs; the portion of Article 14 (2) preceding the subparagraphs; the portion of Article 15 (1) preceding the subparagraphs and Article 15 (2); the portions of Article 16 (1) and (2) preceding the subparagraphs; Article 17 (1) and the portions of Article 17 (2) and (3) preceding the subparagraphs; the portion of Article 19 preceding the subparagraphs; Article 21 (1) and the portion of Article 21 (3) preceding the subparagraphs; the portions of Article 23 (1) and (2) preceding the subparagraphs; the portions of Article 24 (1) and (2) preceding the subparagraphs; Article 25 (2); Article 26 (1) 3, (2), and (3); and Article 27 (1) and (2), the former part of Article 27 (3), and the proviso to Article 27 (4), "Minister of Construction and Transportation" shall each be replaced by "Minister of Land, Transport and Maritime Affairs".

In the portion of Article 14 (2) preceding the subparagraphs; the portion of Article 16 (1) preceding the subparagraphs; the portion of Article 19 preceding the subparagraphs; Article 21 (1); the portions of Article 23 (1) and (2) preceding the subparagraphs; and the portion of Article 24 (1) preceding the subparagraphs, "Ordinance of the Ministry of Construction and Transportation" shall each be replaced by "Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Transport and Maritime Affairs".

(81) through (138) Omitted.

ADDENDA (Decree Partially Amending the Enforcement Decree of the Individual Consumption Tax Act and Other Decrees for Joint Use of Administrative Information and Reduction of Documents) <No. 21215, 2008.12.31>

This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.

ADDENDA <No. 21554, 2009.6.25>

This Decree shall enter into force on July 2, 2009.

ADDENDA (Enforcement Decree of the Electronic Government Act) <Presidential Decree No. 22151, May 4, 2010>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on May 5, 2010.

Articles 2 and 3 Omitted.

Article 4 (Amendments to Other Statutes)
